## Objective

Implement the internal, authenticated process-lifecycle primitive that owns one
Codex app-server plus one stock `codex --remote` frontend as a single managed
unit. This task supplies a reusable OCaml API to T006; it does not decide or
publish the user-facing command syntax.

## Scope and non-goals

- Implement only after T001 records positive `protocol` and
  `control_boundary` verdicts for the installed/supported Codex range.
- Own endpoint allocation, authentication/capability setup, child spawning,
  readiness, supervision, exit propagation, cleanup, and the minimal persisted
  mapping needed for later resume/delivery.
- Integrate with the existing managed-instance process infrastructure rather
  than creating a second launcher framework.
- This task does **not** add/change `c2c start codex`, `c2c codex`, `c2c new`,
  `c2c resume`, alias generation/override rules, or `--yolo`. T006 exclusively
  owns public grammar, aliases, generated-name UX, and flag forwarding.
- This task does not deliver c2c messages or call any thread/turn method; T003
  owns passive ingress and T007 owns any policy-driven `turn/start` behavior.

